-- title:
--   Surjectivity of the tower-level Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation on geometric points
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a positive integer $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   Base rings (groups `hdvr`–`hvdet`). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, in which $2$ and $3$ are units, together with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$; a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$. Further, a characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod \pi$ for all $x$. Finally a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   Indefinite quaternionic side and coarse moduli (`hB`, `hΛ`, `h𝒳`, `hgr`, `hgc`). Rationals $a,b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`: $a > 0$ or $b > 0$, and for a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies over $r$ or over $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (an order maximal among the orders containing it). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with $f : \mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and an assignment $\mathrm{pt}$ sending a fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure over a ring $S$, together with a structure morphism $s$, to an $S$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $s$, such that `IsCoarseModuli Λ N 𝒳 f pt` holds: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on points with values in algebraically closed fields up to isomorphism, and the universal property among such point assignments. The generic fibre of $f$, i.e. the second projection of the pullback of $f$ along $\operatorname{Spec} K_0 \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, is geometrically reduced and geometrically connected.
--
--   Full level $n$ (`hM`, `hρ`) and the map to $\mathcal X$ (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`). An integer $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; a scheme $M$ with $fM : M \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a point assignment $\mathrm{ptF}$ on fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure satisfying `IsFineModuli` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, surjectivity and injectivity on $S$-points up to isomorphism); a group $G$ with $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ and $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ such that `IsLevelTwistAction` holds, i.e. $\rho$ acts over the base, $\mathrm{ptF}$ of a $\chi(h)$-twist equals $\mathrm{ptF}$ followed by $\rho(h)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n$ in the sense spelled out there. A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ with $p$ followed by $f$ equal to $fM$, invariant under all $\rho(h)$, and carrying full-level points to the corresponding coarse points.
--
--   The Hecke tower (`h𝒴`, `hgrT`, `hgcT`, `hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`). For every prime $\ell \neq r, \bar r$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with $g_\ell : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a point assignment $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ on fake elliptic curves with an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup satisfying `IsCoarseModuliT` (the same five clauses for level-$\ell$ data); the generic fibre of each $g_\ell$ is geometrically reduced and geometrically connected; degeneracy morphisms $d_0\ell, d_1\ell : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base, $d_0\ell$ forgetting the extra level and $d_1\ell$ computing the $\ell$-isogenous quotient in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsLevelIsogeny`.
--
--   Atkin–Lehner morphisms (`har`, `harbar`). Endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base which on points send a fake elliptic curve to any Atkin–Lehner quotient at $r$, respectively at $\bar r$.
--
--   Definite quaternionic side (`hdef`–`hwbar`). Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt rbar`: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the place over $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ with $R_1 \leq \Lambda_1$; an adelic unit $n_1$ in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,R_1\,r$ such that $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ is Eichler of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0 : \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$; the place $v$ over $r$; a subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of the units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ whose elements are exactly those of `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`. For each tower prime $\ell$, units $s_\ell$ and adelic units $sf_\ell$ such that $sf_\ell$ is the diagonal image of $s_\ell$ at every place not over $r$ and is $1$ at the place over $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_1\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1)\,\ell$ if $\ell \mid N$ and in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1)\,\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; and $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$. A unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$.
--
--   Uniformisation data at full level and in the tower. A group homomorphism $\theta_t : \Gamma_t \to G$; for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map $\Theta_f$ from triples consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr \to B$, a Deligne datum in $(\mathrm{Omega}\,K_0\,\pi)(B)$ and an element of $G$, to the $B$-points of $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$; and for each tower prime $\ell$ a map $\Theta_{T,\ell}$ from pairs (coefficient map, Deligne datum) to the $B$-points of $\mathcal Y_\ell$. These satisfy: `hnat`, naturality of $\Theta_f$ in $B$; `hG`, $\rho(h)$ applied to $\Theta_f(x, gh)$ equals $\Theta_f(x,g)$; `hinv`, $\Theta_f(x', \theta_t(\gamma)g) = \Theta_f(x,g)$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ and $x'$ is obtained from $x$ by the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ (Frobenius twist of the coefficient map by $-\mathrm{vdet}$ together with pullback of the Deligne datum); `het`, unique lifting of points along a surjection $B \to B_0$ of $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebras whose kernel satisfies that any two elements mapping to $0$ have zero product; `hfib`, the fibre criterion stating that $\Theta_f((\psi,P),g) = \Theta_f((\psi',P'),g')$ over an algebraically closed $\pi$-nilpotent field $k$ holds if and only if there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ with $g' = \theta_t(\gamma)g$, with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ under $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and with $\psi'$ agreeing with the $(-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma))$-fold Frobenius twist of $\psi$ on every $y \in Onr$ fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0 z)}$ for all scalar $z \in \Gamma_t$ with $\theta_t(z) = 1$; `hsurj`, for every algebraically closed $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-field $k$, every $\psi$ and every $k$-point $y$ of $M$ there are $P$ and $g$ with $\Theta_f((\psi,P),g) = y$; `hnatT` and `hiT`, naturality and $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$-invariance of $\Theta_{T,\ell}$; `hfibT`, the fibre criterion for $\Theta_{T,\ell}$ at a fixed coefficient map, with $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ in place of $\Gamma_t$; and `hiv0`, that $\Theta_{T,\ell}$ followed by $d_0\ell$ equals $\Theta_f(\cdot\,,1)$ followed by $p$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every prime $\ell \neq r, \bar r$, and for every level-$\ell$ fine package over it, namely a scheme $M_\ell$ with $fM_\ell : M_\ell \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and an assignment $\mathrm{ptF}_\ell$ on pairs (fake elliptic curve with full level-$n$ structure, extra level-$\ell$ subgroup) satisfying `IsFineModuliT Λ N n ℓ`, a morphism $\pi_\ell : M_\ell \to M$ over the base compatible with the point assignments, a morphism $p_\ell : M_\ell \to \mathcal Y_\ell$ over the base compatible with the point assignments, and a homomorphism $\rho_\ell : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M_\ell$ acting over the base, intertwining $\pi_\ell$ with $\rho$, fixing $p_\ell$, and such that for each $h \in G$ and each isomorphism $e$ exhibiting $u'$ as the $\chi(h)$-twist of $u$ in the sense of `WithFullLevel.IsTwistVia` which matches the extra level subgroups $C$ and $C'$ (a point factors through $C$ exactly when its image factors through $C'$), one has $\mathrm{ptF}_\ell(u',C') = \mathrm{ptF}_\ell(u,C)$ followed by $\rho_\ell(h)$; and for every map $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ into the $\pi$-nilpotent points of $fM_\ell$ satisfying the same clauses as $\Theta_f$, namely naturality, the $G$-equivariance $\rho_\ell(h)\Theta_{f,\ell}(x,gh) = \Theta_{f,\ell}(x,g)$, invariance under the twisted action of $\gamma \in \Gamma_t \cap \Gamma_{t,\ell}$ through $\theta_t$, the unique-lifting property along surjections as above, the fibre criterion with the additional requirement $\gamma \in \Gamma_{t,\ell}$, and the compatibilities that $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ followed by $\pi_\ell$ equals $\Theta_f$ and that $\Theta_{f,\ell}(\cdot\,,1)$ followed by $p_\ell$ equals $\Theta_{T,\ell}$ — the following two assertions hold.
--
--   First: for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with nilpotent image of $\pi$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : Onr \to k$ and every $k$-point $y$ of $M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, there exist a Deligne datum $P \in (\mathrm{Omega}\,K_0\,\pi)(k)$ and an element $g \in G$ with $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g) = y$.
--
--   Second: for every such $k$ and $\psi$ and every $k$-point $y$ of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, there exists a Deligne datum $P \in (\mathrm{Omega}\,K_0\,\pi)(k)$ with $\Theta_{T,\ell}(\psi,P) = y$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation at the tower level: it upgrades surjectivity on geometric points from the fine moduli scheme of full level $n$ to the level-$(n,\ell)$ fine scheme $M_\ell$ and to the coarse level-$\ell$ scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ of the Hecke tower, for every prime $\ell$ away from the two ramified primes. It is used in assembling the full uniformisation package carrying the Atkin–Lehner morphisms at $r$ and $\bar r$ together with the tower structure.
